Finished with 24600 points, which was minscore for the dungeon depth I
was given (47).
Wished up a pet Archon, but my vampire lord with +5 elf boots, "oR and
DSM was just as loyal a companion, and made it to Astral with me.

Plenty of tripe in soko meant I had 4 maxed cats and a dog by the time
I found a polytrap, which gave me a Titan that stuck around for quite
a while before eating a chameleon and becoming a nymph.  Also got that
vampire and a hasted baluchitherium (the latter eventually starved, as
all my vegetarian pets tend to...)

Early magic whistle and CoMR from bones and SDSM from a dragon I lured
through the quest portal made the early game easy enough all the way
to the castle wand that gave me the PYEC and let me switch to robe.  A
dwarf drinking a !oGL in plain sight made leveling up past XL1 less
hassle than it had been in previous attempts.  Minetown bookstore had
a level 3 spellbook that turned out to be identify, which is pretty
much crucial in a minscore game.

Nothing all that eventful in a tedious game (an ill-considered "new
gnome" experience to get rid of an unwanted polytrap in a maze dropped
me back from XL3 to 1, which was Really Annoying), until, being almost
ready to take on Rodney,  I stupidly quaffed from a fountain in the
hopes of getting my casting skills for remove curse down to 0% and
ended up with a cursed BoH with all the uncursing tools inside.  It
was too heavy to cast remove curse while wielding it so I had to go up
16 levels to my stash and grab a cancel wand.

Only ever misplaced my Archon via levelport once, and that was in the
quest, so he didn't have very far he could go.  Ascension run wasn't
too bad despite the mysterious force.  The high priest dropped a c!
oGL, which was handy.  Yeenoghu appeared, at some point, not sure how,
but was duly dispatched.  Rodney appeared 7 times, and I eventually
had to hit him 3 times with the Staff to get him down to a point where
my pet would attack him - each move terrifying in case he nicked it
off me.

Found a magic harp just before I hit DL1, which made the elemental
planes a doddle.  Used it to great effects against the swarms of 'a'
on Astral too.  Second altar was mine - guarded by pestillence, which
made me glad of my !oFH stack.  Stupidly used my magic whistle to try
and move my Archon 2 or more squares away from me at the high altar
(turns out I'd never taken the leash off him) and got surrounded by my
pet ants that would have given me points I didn't want.  Took a while
to convince them all to beat each other to death or leave, all the
while dancing with pestillence.

Eventually I got to a point where I could drop all my amulets and
artifacts, which left me AoLS- and MR-less for one nerve-racking
turn.  My Archon wandered off with the PYEC, which is kind of a nice
touch.  I offered the amulet and ascended.

I don't know what it says about me that I enjoy this kind of tedium
much more than trying to speed up my ascension turn count, but I had
fun.  It'd be nice if NAO could be patched not to give you DL-based
points below level 45 though, so you're not completely at the mercy of
the RNG regarding the minimum possible score.

